#: src/network/interactive_games.py:295
msgid ""
"Tip: instead of typing rules here, drop a folder via 'Add folder...'. Any"
" .txt/.md at the root becomes the main rules. Subfolders such as "
"objects/, classes/, quests/, npcs/ become labeled entity catalogs the AI "
"references during play."
msgstr ""

#: src/network/interactive_games.py:306
msgid ""
"The server keeps score for you, so you can write rules that rely on it: "
"world variables (the weather, a quest stage), each player's statistics "
"(hit points, strength, gold, ammunition) with the arithmetic and the "
"limits done server-side, what every player is carrying and wearing, dice "
"rolls, and skill checks the server decides rather than the AI. Just say "
"what your game needs - \"everyone starts with 12 hit points and a bow\", "
"\"a locked door needs a strength check against 10\" - and the game master"
" will use the right one."
msgstr ""

